PrimePC Privacy Policy

Last updated: October 2, 2026

PrimePC is a Windows desktop application that helps users find, download, and install software. This Privacy Policy explains how PrimePC handles information when you use the application.
Information PrimePC Collects

PrimePC does not intentionally collect, create user accounts for, or store personal information such as your name, email address, passwords, contacts, photos, or documents.

PrimePC does not require you to provide personal information in order to use its core functionality.
Downloads and Third-Party Websites

PrimePC may connect to third-party websites or software distribution services to download application installers. Those services may receive information that is normally transmitted when a device connects to a website or server, such as an IP address, browser or application information, and request information. Their handling of information is governed by their own privacy policies.

PrimePC does not control the privacy practices of third-party software publishers or download servers. Users should review the applicable privacy policies and terms of those services when appropriate.
Application Installation

PrimePC can launch software installers selected by the user. Some installers may require administrator approval through Windows User Account Control (UAC). PrimePC does not intentionally bypass Windows security prompts or obtain administrator privileges without the user's authorization.
Local Files and Settings

PrimePC may access files and folders that are necessary for downloading, caching, running, or installing software. Information used for these purposes remains on the user's device unless it is transmitted as part of a connection to a third-party download or software service.
Analytics, Advertising, and Tracking

PrimePC does not intentionally include advertising or user-tracking functionality as part of its core application.
Children's Privacy

PrimePC is not specifically directed toward children. PrimePC does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated if PrimePC's functionality or data practices change. The updated version will be published at the same location, and the "Last updated" date will be changed accordingly.
Data Security

PrimePC does not intentionally collect or maintain a database of users' personal information. Users should still use appropriate Windows security practices and only install software from sources they trust.
Contact

PrimePC does not provide a separate contact address through this Privacy Policy. 
